              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "To log in to Microsoft OneDrive, you can use any of the following methods depending on your device:\n\n### 1. On a Web Browser (Computer, Tablet, or Phone)\n1. Go directly to the official **[OneDrive Login Page](https://onedrive.live.com)**.\n2. Click the **Sign in** button.\n3. Enter your **Microsoft account email address** or phone number (this is the same email you use for Outlook, Xbox, or Windows).\n4. Click **Next** and enter your **password**. \n5. If you have two-factor authentication enabled, verify your identity using your authentication app or a code sent to your phone/email.\n\n---\n\n### 2. On Windows (Desktop App)\nOneDrive is pre-installed on most Windows computers.\n1. Click the **Windows Start Menu** (or press the Windows Key) and type `OneDrive`. \n2. Click on the **OneDrive app** from the search results to open it.\n3. If it is your first time opening it, a window will pop up asking you to enter your email address. \n4. Enter your Microsoft account details to sign in and start syncing your folders. \n\n*(If OneDrive is already running, you can find the **cloud icon** in your taskbar near the bottom-right clock. Click it, select the settings gear icon, and go to **Account** > **Add an account**).*\n\n---\n\n### 3. On macOS (Mac App)\n1. If you haven't installed it, download OneDrive from the Mac App Store.\n2. Open **Finder**, go to **Applications**, and launch **OneDrive**.\n3. Enter your Microsoft account email and password to log in and sync your files.\n\n---\n\n### 4. On Mobile Devices (iOS or Android)\n1. Download the official **Microsoft OneDrive** app from the [Apple App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/microsoft-onedrive/id823766827) or [Google Play Store](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.microsoft.skydrive).\n2. Open the app and sign in using your Microsoft account details.",
